  m_Name: ChickenInfo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  displayName: Chicken
  category: 1
  summary: Chickens are farm birds raised for eggs and meat. They come from the wild
    red jungle fowl of India!
  facts:
  - There are more than 60 breeds of chickens!
  - Chickens have a pecking order, a ranking that decides who gets to eat first!
  - Fluffy chicks grow all their feathers in just 4 to 5 weeks!
  - Free-range chickens can live 6 to 8 years.
  sources:
  - Encyclopaedia Britannica. Chicken. https://www.britannica.com/animal/chicken
